  "visualBrief": "Closed-shutter Spreckels Organ Pavilion: native central rectangular organ house and U-shaped paired-row Corinthian colonnades/terminal portals. Giant round arch with true pierced original floral rosettes/petal tracery and raised moldings, inset ribbed shutter, decorated lower pilasters/plain inset plaques/door+transom bays and shell pediments. Curved triangular central parapet/shell cornice/urns, twin side window recesses/round louver/curved crest and lower barred side entry. Open colonnade bays/coffered ceiling/turned-baluster parapets/urn piers; free terminal columns/flanking relief piers/segmental portal crest/urns and north stairs. Stage apron/paired side stair flights retain independent ground, no plaza seating/fountain/neighbors/interior/organ pipes/flags/art text.",
